# =============================================================================
# XyScript UI string table  —  TRANSLATION TEMPLATE
# =============================================================================
#
# This is a flat, human-editable catalog of XyScript's user-interface strings.
# To make a non-English build, COPY this file to  xyscript-strings-<lang>.txt
# (e.g. xyscript-strings-fr.txt), fill in a translation after each " = ", and
# select it at runtime.  Nothing here is compiled — it's plain UTF-8 text.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   key = translation                 # English source (reference)
#
#   * One entry per line: everything left of the FIRST "=" is the key; the rest
#     (trimmed) is the translation.
#   * The trailing "# ..." on each line is the English SOURCE, shown so you know
#     what to translate. The loader ignores it. Leave it in place.
#   * A BLANK translation falls back to the English source, so you can translate
#     incrementally and ship a partial catalog.
#   * Lines starting with "#" and blank lines are comments.
#   * Encoding is UTF-8. Accented/non-Latin text is fine.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS
#   Some strings contain a {name} placeholder that the program fills in at run
#   time (a number, a filename, …). Keep every {name} EXACTLY as written; you
#   may move it to wherever your language needs it.
#       menu.view.wrap_hang = Retrait suspendu ({n})…   # Wrap hang ({n})…
#
# WHAT IS NOT HERE (on purpose)
#   * COMMAND VERBS (OPEN, SAVE, GREP, …) are the command LANGUAGE, not UI text.
#     They stay English so scripts, key bindings, and the manual work in every
#     locale. Menu items still trigger those verbs; only the visible LABEL is
#     translated here.
#   * Dynamically generated items (encoding names, syntax token-kind names,
#     etc.) are not listed — they come from data tables, handled separately.
#   * The manual / reference (docs/reference.typ) is a separate, larger effort.
#
# SCOPE OF THIS FILE
#   Section 1 (MENUS) is the complete menu-bar inventory — the phase-1 target.
#   Sections 2–3 (DIALOGS, MESSAGES) are ILLUSTRATIVE STUBS showing how the same
#   scheme extends; they are not yet exhaustive.
# =============================================================================


